  data: {
    LLM: "Calculate your 'Safe' tricks. In Preferans, bidding is about certainty, not hope. If you have the Ace and King of a suit, that is two safe tricks. If you have 5 trumps including the Ace, you can safely bid 6. Be extremely careful with 'Misere'â€”it is high-risk, high-reward, and the defenders will play 'Crucial Card' logic to force you to take a trick.\n\nWhistling Discipline: Only 'Whistle' if you have 'Stop cards' (Aces or Kings). If you Whistle and fail (Get set), you lose massive points on the 'Mountain'. However, Whistling is the only way to earn 'Whist points'â€”the most valuable currency in the final score calculation. It is the art of knowing when to punish the declarer and when to let them win.\n\nThe 'Talon' Discard: The 2 cards you discard after picking up the Widow can win or lose you the game. Protect your weak suits by discarding the low cards of those suits. If you have a 'Void', you have a massive advantage in trumping the declarer's high cards. The best Preferans players treat every hand as a puzzle of 'Optimal Shedding' before the first trick is even played.",
    Player: "Calculate your 'Safe' tricks. In Preferans, bidding is about certainty, not hope. If you have the Ace and King of a suit, that is two safe tricks. If you have 5 trumps including the Ace, you can safely bid 6. Be extremely careful with 'Misere'â€”it is high-risk, high-reward, and the defenders will play 'Crucial Card' logic to force you to take a trick.\n\nWhistling Discipline: Only 'Whistle' if you have 'Stop cards' (Aces or Kings). If you Whistle and fail (Get set), you lose massive points on the 'Mountain'. However, Whistling is the only way to earn 'Whist points'â€”the most valuable currency in the final score calculation. It is the art of knowing when to punish the declarer and when to let them win.\n\nThe 'Talon' Discard: The 2 cards you discard after picking up the Widow can win or lose you the game. Protect your weak suits by discarding the low cards of those suits. If you have a 'Void', you have a massive advantage in trumping the declarer's high cards. The best Preferans players treat every hand as a puzzle of 'Optimal Shedding' before the first trick is even played.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
    bluffFrequency: 0.3,
    bluffSettings: {
      profile: 'balanced',
